g cross-sectional and longitudinal seroconverter specimens from Africa</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>403</fpage><lpage>408</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17301558</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050080-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Podgor</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Leske</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Estimating incidence from age-specific prevalence for irreversible diseases with differential mortality</article-title><source>Stat Med</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>573</fpage><lpage>578</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3823665</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050080-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ades</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Medley</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Estimates of disease incidence in women based on antenatal or neonatal seroprevalence data: HIV in New York City</article-title><source>Stat Med</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>1881</fpage><lpage>1894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7997720</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050080-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ades</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Serial HIV seroprevalence surveys: interpretation, design, and role in HIV/AIDS prediction</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr Hum Retrovirol</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>490</fpage><lpage>499</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7627625</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050080-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sakarovitch</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>A